NAME
       e2fsck - check and repair an ext2, ext3 or ext4 file system (also fsck.ext4)

SYNOPSIS
       e2fsck [-f] [-n] [-p] [-y] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       e2fsck reads an ext4 (or ext2, ext3) file system and checks that its
       structures agree with each other, then fixes what it can. It prints
       the passes it goes through and a summary line with the number of
       files and blocks in use.

       Check only file systems that are not mounted: repairing a mounted
       file system can destroy data. Unmount it first (umount /data), or
       boot into the emergency target for the root file system.

       e2fsck also runs before resize2fs shrinks a file system. fsck.ext4 and
       fsck -t ext4 run this same program.

OPTIONS
       -f     Check even when the file system looks clean.

       -n     Answer no to every question: only report, change nothing.

       -p     Repair simple problems automatically without asking.

       -y     Answer yes to every question.

EXAMPLES
       Check an unmounted ext4 file system, even if it is marked clean:

           umount /data
           e2fsck -f /dev/vdb1

SEE ALSO
       fsck(8), resize2fs(8), tune2fs(8), xfs_repair(8)
